    {
      "id": "852d9da2-0845-477a-9f97-e05746ef5bd2",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        272,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## AI News Classifier\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors an RSS feed for new AI news articles, limits each run to 10 items, and uses Gemini-powered LLM chains to classify and prepare qualifying articles. Articles that pass the conditional check are turned into PostNitro post drafts, then scheduled and followed up with Gmail notifications. It separates the process into intake, AI classification, AI content generation, and publishing confirmation steps.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the RSS Feed Read Trigger with the target AI news feed URL and polling settings.\n- Add Google Gemini credentials for both LLM chain nodes and verify the structured output parser schemas match the prompts.\n- Configure the If node condition to match the classification output that identifies articles worth posting.\n- Connect PostNitro credentials and set the draft generation and scheduling options.\n- Connect Gmail OAuth credentials and set recipient addresses, subjects, and email body templates for both notification emails.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the RSS source, article limit, classification prompt, relevance condition, post-generation prompt, scheduling time, and email templates to fit the desired content strategy."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "58cfb85a-1cd7-4e13-b99b-81092a1af14b",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        800,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 464,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Fetch latest articles\n\nStarts the workflow when the RSS feed updates and caps processing to the first 10 incoming articles."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
